  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shivalinga vs Umesh .M.A on 5 August, 2025 Scch-08 1 Mvc No.4775/2023 c/w. 4776/2023 Kabc020214472023 In The Court Of Xii Addl. Small Cause Judge And Motor Accident Claims Tribunal, Bengaluru. (Scch-08) Dated This The 05th Day Of August - 2025 Present: Smt. Kannika M.S. M.A. Ll.B, Xii Addl. Scj & Acjm, Member - Mact, Bengaluru. Mvc No.4775/2023 c/w. 4776/2023 Petitioner/S Sri Jagadeesh, (in Mvc 4775/23) S/o. Kempe Gowda, Aged about 47 years, R/at No.6, 17th Main, 9th Cross, J.C. Nagar, Kurubarahalli, Mahalakshmi Layout, Bengaluru-86 Petitioner/S Sri Shivalinga, (in Mvc 4776/23) S/o. Ballaiah,",
    "facts": "The petitioners of MVC No.4775/2023 c/w. 4776/2023 have filed these petitions under Section 166 of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1989 seeking compensation for the injuries sustained by them in the road traffic accident occurred on 22.06.2023. The petitioner of MVC No.4775/2023 has filed application to club MVC No.4776/2023 with it. The said application came to be allowed on the ground that the respondents in both the cases are one and the same and the injuries were caused from the same accident. Hence, both these cases are clubbed together to lead common evidence. 3. The brief facts of the case of the petitioners as follow:- On 22.06.2023 at about 5.15 p.m. when they were travelling in a Private Bus bearing Reg. No. KA-51-AG-206 as passengers, on Manvi Sindanur road, near Nasalapur bridge, Manvi Taluk, Raichur District, the driver of the said bus driven the same with high speed and in a rash and negligent manner dashed against the motor cycle which was coming from opposite direction. After hitting the motor cycle, the driver lost control over the bus and then hit the safety iron sheet fixed on side of the road, caused the accident and as a result, they sustained grievous injuries. It is contended that, immediately they were taken to nearby Govt. hospital, Manvi, wherein they were taken first aid, thereafter for higher treatment they were shifted to Fortis hospital, Bengaluru, wherein they took treatment as an inpatient. It is SCCH-08 4 MVC No.4775/2023 c/w. 4776/2023 contended that they have spent huge amount for treatment and medical expenses. 4. It is further stated that prior to the accident, petitioners in MVC No.4775/2023 and 4776/2023 were hale and healthy and petitioner in MVC No.4775/20223 was owner cum driver of 407 Goods vehicle and was earning sum of Rs.50,000/- p.m. and the petitioner in MVC No.4776/2023 was working as Electrician and was earning sum of Rs.24,000/- p.m. Due to the accidental injuries, they are unable to do their work as doing earlier. It is stated that the accident in question was due to the rash and negligence on the part of the driver of the private bus bearing Reg. No. KA-51-AG-206. Hence, the 1st respondent being the owner and 2nd respondent being the insurer of the offending vehicle are jointly and severally liable to pay the compensation. 5. Inspite of service of summons, the 1 st respondent remained exparte. On service of notice, 2 nd respondent appeared before the court through its counsel and filed separate written statements. Shivalinga vs Umesh .M.A on 5 August, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/97836050/ 3 6. The 2nd respondent in its objections has stated that the petitions are not maintainable either in law or on facts and hence the petitions are liable to be dismissed for non joinder of necessary parties. This respondent has denied the issuance of policy in favour of respondent No.1 in respect of the offending Bus bearing Reg No. KA-51-AG-0206 and the liability if any is subject to the terms and conditions of the policy. Further stated that, the petitioners sustained injuries due to the negligent act of the rider of motor cycle who was riding the said motor cycle in a rash and negligent SCCH-08 5 MVC No.4775/2023 c/w. 4776/2023 manner on narrow Bridge. Further stated that the rider of the motor cycle was not having DL and policy in respect of motor cycle. The police authorities not complied the provisions as contemplated u/s 158(6) of MV Act. Further stated that the owner of the bus allowed many persons to travel in the bus exceeding its capacity and violated the terms and conditions of the policy. Further stated that the driver of the private bus was driving the vehicle without possessing a valid and effective driving licence, FC and Permit. It has denied the age, occupation and income, period of hospitalization and treatment taken by the petitioners.",
    "arguments": "It is contended that the compensation claimed by the petitioners is high exorbitant. On other grounds pray for dismissal of the petitions. The multiplier applicable to the age of 55 is 11 as per the case of Sarla Verma and others vs. Delhi Transport Corporation(AIR 2009 SC 3104). Shivalinga vs Umesh .M.A on 5 August, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/97836050/ 10 Hence, petitioner is entitled for the compensation of Rs.1,05,600/-(Rs.16,000x12x11x5/100) towards loss of future income on account of permanent disability. 23. PAIN AND SUFFERINGS: Our Hon'ble High Court in the case rendered in Vijay Ishwar Jadhav and others Vs Ulrich Belchior Fernandes and another (MFA.No.100090/2014 C/W MFA.No.25107/2013 dated Shivalinga vs Umesh .M.A on 5 August, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/97836050/ 12 07.03.2018), has held that in the absence of any other law relating to interest on judgments, the MACT has to follow the provisions of Sec.34 of C.P.C and awarded interest @ 6% p.a.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "It is contended that the compensation claimed by the petitioners is high exorbitant. On other grounds pray for dismissal of the petitions.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "The multiplier applicable to the age of 55 is 11 as per the case of Sarla Verma and others vs. Delhi Transport Corporation(AIR 2009 SC 3104). Shivalinga vs Umesh .M.A on 5 August, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/97836050/ 10 Hence, petitioner is entitled for the compensation of Rs.1,05,600/-(Rs.16,000x12x11x5/100) towards loss of future income on account of permanent disability. 23. PAIN AND SUFFERINGS: Our Hon'ble High Court in the case rendered in Vijay Ishwar Jadhav and others Vs Ulrich Belchior Fernandes and another (MFA.No.100090/2014 C/W MFA.No.25107/2013 dated Shivalinga vs Umesh .M.A on 5 August, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/97836050/ 12 07.03.2018), has held that in the absence of any other law relating to interest on judgments, the MACT has to follow the provisions of Sec.34 of C.P.C and awarded interest @ 6% p.a."
  },
